# C# and .NET Coding Standards

## Context

Apply when writing C# code for the ASP.NET Core 9 backend. These standards ensure consistency, maintainability, and quality across the codebase.

## Requirements

### Language Features

- **USE** C# 13 features:
  - File-scoped namespaces
  - Record types for DTOs
  - Pattern matching
  - Nullable reference types (strict mode)
  - Required properties
  - Init-only setters for immutability
- **USE** `var` for local variables when type is obvious from right side
- **USE** expression-bodied members for simple methods/properties
- **USE** string interpolation instead of `String.Format` or concatenation
- **AVOID** `dynamic` type unless absolutely necessary

### Naming Conventions

- **PascalCase**: Classes, methods, properties, public fields, namespaces
- **camelCase**: Private fields (with `_` prefix), parameters, local variables
- **UPPERCASE_SNAKE_CASE**: Constants
- **I{Name}**: Interfaces (e.g., `IUserService`)
- **{Name}Dto**: Data Transfer Objects
- **{Name}Entity** or just **{Name}**: Domain entities

```csharp
// ✅ Good
public class UserService : IUserService
{
    private readonly ILogger<UserService> _logger;
    private const int MAX_RETRY_ATTEMPTS = 3;

    public async Task<UserDto> GetUserByIdAsync(Guid userId)
    {
        var user = await _repository.GetByIdAsync(userId);
        return _mapper.Map<UserDto>(user);
    }
}

// ❌ Bad
public class userService : iUserService  // Wrong casing
{
    private ILogger<UserService> logger;  // Missing underscore
    private const int maxRetryAttempts = 3;  // Should be UPPERCASE

    public async Task<UserDto> getUserById(Guid user_id)  // Wrong casing
    {
        // ...
    }
}
```

### File Organization

- **ONE** public type per file
- File name matches the type name
- File-scoped namespaces (no extra indentation)
- Using directives at top, sorted alphabetically
- Order members: constants → fields → constructors → properties → methods

```csharp
// ✅ Good: PredictionService.cs
using AutoMapper;
using FootballPrediction.Domain.Entities;
using FootballPrediction.Domain.Interfaces;
using Microsoft.Extensions.Logging;

namespace FootballPrediction.Application.Services;

public class PredictionService : IPredictionService
{
    private const int MAX_PREDICTIONS_PER_USER = 100;

    private readonly IPredictionRepository _repository;
    private readonly ILogger<PredictionService> _logger;
    private readonly IMapper _mapper;

    public PredictionService(
        IPredictionRepository repository,
        ILogger<PredictionService> logger,
        IMapper mapper)
    {
        _repository = repository;
        _logger = logger;
        _mapper = mapper;
    }

    public async Task<PredictionDto> CreateAsync(CreatePredictionDto dto)
    {
        // Implementation
    }
}
```

### Dependency Injection

- **ALWAYS** use constructor injection
- **NEVER** use field injection
- **NEVER** use service locator pattern
- Register services in `Program.cs` with appropriate lifetime:
  - `AddSingleton` - Single instance for app lifetime
  - `AddScoped` - One instance per request
  - `AddTransient` - New instance every time

```csharp
// ✅ Good: Constructor injection
public class UserController : ControllerBase
{
    private readonly IUserService _userService;

    public UserController(IUserService userService)
    {
        _userService = userService;
    }
}

// ❌ Bad: Field injection or service locator
public class UserController : ControllerBase
{
    [Inject]  // Don't do this
    private IUserService _userService;

    // Or this
    public UserController(IServiceProvider serviceProvider)
    {
        _userService = serviceProvider.GetService<IUserService>();
    }
}
```

### Async/Await

- **ALWAYS** use async/await for I/O operations
- **SUFFIX** async methods with `Async`
- **USE** `ConfigureAwait(false)` in library code (not needed in ASP.NET Core)
- **AVOID** `async void` (use `async Task` instead, except event handlers)
- **AVOID** mixing sync and async code

```csharp
// ✅ Good
public async Task<User> GetUserAsync(Guid id)
{
    var user = await _repository.GetByIdAsync(id);
    return user;
}

// ❌ Bad
public User GetUserAsync(Guid id)  // Not async but named Async
{
    var user = _repository.GetByIdAsync(id).Result;  // Blocking
    return user;
}

public async void SaveUserAsync(User user)  // async void (bad)
{
    await _repository.SaveAsync(user);
}
```

### Null Safety

- **ENABLE** nullable reference types (`<Nullable>enable</Nullable>`)
- **USE** `?` for nullable types
- **USE** null-coalescing operators (`??`, `??=`)
- **USE** null-conditional operators (`?.`, `?[]`)
- **AVOID** explicit null checks when nullable annotations prevent nulls

```csharp
// ✅ Good
public class User
{
    public required string Email { get; init; }  // Non-nullable, required
    public string? PhoneNumber { get; init; }    // Nullable, optional

    public string GetDisplayName()
    {
        return PhoneNumber ?? "N/A";  // Null-coalescing
    }
}

// ❌ Bad
public class User
{
    public string Email { get; init; }  // Missing 'required'
    public string PhoneNumber { get; init; }  // Should be nullable

    public string GetDisplayName()
    {
        if (PhoneNumber == null)  // Unnecessary check if properly annotated
            return "N/A";
        return PhoneNumber;
    }
}
```

### Error Handling

- **USE** specific exception types, not generic `Exception`
- **CREATE** custom exceptions for domain-specific errors
- **LOG** exceptions with sufficient context
- **NEVER** catch exceptions without handling or logging
- **NEVER** swallow exceptions silently
- **USE** global exception handler for unhandled exceptions

```csharp
// ✅ Good
public async Task<Prediction> CreatePredictionAsync(CreatePredictionDto dto)
{
    try
    {
        var match = await _matchRepository.GetByIdAsync(dto.MatchId);
        if (match is null)
        {
            throw new NotFoundException($"Match {dto.MatchId} not found");
        }

        if (match.KickoffTime <= DateTime.UtcNow)
        {
            throw new PredictionDeadlineException("Cannot predict after kickoff");
        }

        // Create prediction
        return prediction;
    }
    catch (DbUpdateException ex)
    {
        _logger.LogError(ex, "Database error creating prediction for match {MatchId}", dto.MatchId);
        throw new DataAccessException("Failed to save prediction", ex);
    }
}

// ❌ Bad
public async Task<Prediction> CreatePredictionAsync(CreatePredictionDto dto)
{
    try
    {
        // Implementation
        return prediction;
    }
    catch (Exception)  // Too broad
    {
        // Silently swallowing exception
        return null;
    }
}
```

### LINQ and Collections

- **USE** LINQ for data transformations
- **USE** method syntax over query syntax (unless query is more readable)
- **AVOID** multiple enumerations (use `.ToList()` if needed)
- **USE** `IEnumerable<T>` for lazy evaluation
- **USE** `IReadOnlyCollection<T>` or `IReadOnlyList<T>` for immutable collections

```csharp
// ✅ Good
public IEnumerable<PredictionDto> GetUserPredictions(Guid userId)
{
    return _predictions
        .Where(p => p.UserId == userId)
        .OrderBy(p => p.Match.KickoffTime)
        .Select(p => _mapper.Map<PredictionDto>(p));
}

// ❌ Bad
public IEnumerable<PredictionDto> GetUserPredictions(Guid userId)
{
    var predictions = _predictions.Where(p => p.UserId == userId);
    var count = predictions.Count();  // First enumeration
    var sorted = predictions.OrderBy(p => p.Match.KickoffTime);  // Second enumeration
    return sorted.Select(p => _mapper.Map<PredictionDto>(p));
}
```

### Entity Framework Core

- **USE** async methods (`.ToListAsync()`, `.FirstOrDefaultAsync()`)
- **USE** `.Include()` for eager loading
- **USE** `.AsNoTracking()` for read-only queries
- **AVOID** N+1 queries (use eager loading)
- **USE** transactions for multi-step operations

```csharp
// ✅ Good
public async Task<IEnumerable<Match>> GetMatchesWithPredictionsAsync(Guid userId)
{
    return await _context.Matches
        .Include(m => m.Predictions.Where(p => p.UserId == userId))
        .Include(m => m.GameWeek)
        .AsNoTracking()
        .ToListAsync();
}

// ❌ Bad
public async Task<IEnumerable<Match>> GetMatchesWithPredictionsAsync(Guid userId)
{
    var matches = await _context.Matches.ToListAsync();  // N+1 query coming
    foreach (var match in matches)
    {
        // This triggers separate query for each match
        match.Predictions = await _context.Predictions
            .Where(p => p.MatchId == match.Id && p.UserId == userId)
            .ToListAsync();
    }
    return matches;
}
```

### API Controllers

- **INHERIT** from `ControllerBase` (not `Controller` for APIs)
- **USE** `[ApiController]` attribute
- **USE** attribute routing `[Route("api/v1/[controller]")]`
- **USE** HTTP method attributes `[HttpGet]`, `[HttpPost]`, etc.
- **RETURN** `IActionResult` or `ActionResult<T>`
- **USE** `[Authorize]` for protected endpoints

```csharp
// ✅ Good
[ApiController]
[Route("api/v1/[controller]")]
[Authorize]
public class PredictionsController : ControllerBase
{
    private readonly IPredictionService _service;

    public PredictionsController(IPredictionService service)
    {
        _service = service;
    }

    [HttpGet("my")]
    public async Task<ActionResult<IEnumerable<PredictionDto>>> GetMyPredictions()
    {
        var userId = User.FindFirst(ClaimTypes.NameIdentifier)?.Value;
        var predictions = await _service.GetUserPredictionsAsync(Guid.Parse(userId));
        return Ok(predictions);
    }

    [HttpPost]
    public async Task<ActionResult<PredictionDto>> Create([FromBody] CreatePredictionDto dto)
    {
        var prediction = await _service.CreateAsync(dto);
        return CreatedAtAction(nameof(GetById), new { id = prediction.Id }, prediction);
    }
}

// ❌ Bad
public class PredictionsController : Controller  // Wrong base class
{
    [HttpGet]
    public PredictionDto[] GetMyPredictions()  // Not async, wrong return type
    {
        var predictions = _service.GetUserPredictions();
        return predictions.ToArray();
    }
}
```

### Validation

- **USE** FluentValidation for complex validation
- **USE** data annotations for simple validation
- **VALIDATE** at API boundary (DTOs)
- **NEVER** skip validation

```csharp
// ✅ Good: FluentValidation
public class CreatePredictionValidator : AbstractValidator<CreatePredictionDto>
{
    public CreatePredictionValidator()
    {
        RuleFor(x => x.HomeScore)
            .InclusiveBetween(0, 9)
            .WithMessage("Home score must be between 0 and 9");

        RuleFor(x => x.AwayScore)
            .InclusiveBetween(0, 9)
            .WithMessage("Away score must be between 0 and 9");

        RuleFor(x => x.MatchId)
            .NotEmpty()
            .WithMessage("Match ID is required");
    }
}

// ✅ Good: Data Annotations
public class CreatePredictionDto
{
    [Required]
    public Guid MatchId { get; init; }

    [Range(0, 9)]
    public int HomeScore { get; init; }

    [Range(0, 9)]
    public int AwayScore { get; init; }
}
```

### Logging

- **USE** `ILogger<T>` with dependency injection
- **USE** structured logging with named parameters
- **AVOID** string interpolation in log messages
- **LOG** at appropriate levels (Trace, Debug, Information, Warning, Error, Critical)
- **NEVER** log sensitive data (passwords, tokens)

```csharp
// ✅ Good
_logger.LogInformation(
    "User {UserId} created prediction {PredictionId} for match {MatchId}",
    userId, predictionId, matchId
);

// ❌ Bad
_logger.LogInformation(
    $"User {userId} created prediction {predictionId} for match {matchId}"
);
```

### Records vs Classes

- **USE** `record` for DTOs (immutable data transfer)
- **USE** `record` for value objects
- **USE** `class` for entities with identity
- **USE** `class` for services

```csharp
// ✅ Good: DTOs as records
public record UserDto(Guid Id, string Username, string Email);

public record CreatePredictionDto
{
    public required Guid MatchId { get; init; }
    public required int HomeScore { get; init; }
    public required int AwayScore { get; init; }
}

// ✅ Good: Entities as classes
public class User
{
    public Guid Id { get; init; }
    public required string Username { get; set; }
    public required string Email { get; set; }
    public string PasswordHash { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}
```

### Testing

- **USE** xUnit for test framework
- **USE** FluentAssertions for readable assertions
- **USE** Moq for mocking
- **NAME** tests: `MethodName_Scenario_ExpectedBehavior`
- **ARRANGE-ACT-ASSERT** pattern

```csharp
// ✅ Good
public class ScoringServiceTests
{
    [Theory]
    [InlineData(2, 1, 2, 1, 5)] // Exact score
    [InlineData(1, 0, 2, 1, 4)] // Winner + diff
    [InlineData(2, 0, 3, 1, 3)] // Winner only
    public void CalculatePoints_ValidPrediction_ReturnsCorrectPoints(
        int predHome, int predAway, int actHome, int actAway, int expected)
    {
        // Arrange
        var service = new ScoringService();

        // Act
        var result = service.CalculatePoints(predHome, predAway, actHome, actAway);

        // Assert
        result.Should().Be(expected);
    }
}
```

## Examples

### Good Practices

```csharp
// ✅ File-scoped namespace
namespace FootballPrediction.Application.Services;

// ✅ Record for DTO
public record PredictionDto
{
    public required Guid Id { get; init; }
    public required Guid MatchId { get; init; }
    public required int HomeScore { get; init; }
    public required int AwayScore { get; init; }
    public int? PointsEarned { get; init; }
}

// ✅ Proper service implementation
public class PredictionService : IPredictionService
{
    private readonly IPredictionRepository _repository;
    private readonly ILogger<PredictionService> _logger;

    public PredictionService(
        IPredictionRepository repository,
        ILogger<PredictionService> logger)
    {
        _repository = repository;
        _logger = logger;
    }

    public async Task<PredictionDto> GetByIdAsync(Guid id)
    {
        var prediction = await _repository
            .GetByIdAsync(id)
            .ConfigureAwait(false);

        if (prediction is null)
        {
            throw new NotFoundException($"Prediction {id} not found");
        }

        return MapToDto(prediction);
    }

    private static PredictionDto MapToDto(Prediction prediction) =>
        new()
        {
            Id = prediction.Id,
            MatchId = prediction.MatchId,
            HomeScore = prediction.HomeScore,
            AwayScore = prediction.AwayScore,
            PointsEarned = prediction.PointsEarned
        };
}
```

## Critical Rules

- **ENABLE** nullable reference types in all projects
- **ALWAYS** use async/await for I/O operations
- **NEVER** use `dynamic` or `object` when proper typing is possible
- **NEVER** use field injection, always constructor injection
- **ALWAYS** validate input at API boundaries
- **ALWAYS** log errors with context
- **USE** records for DTOs, classes for entities
- **FOLLOW** established patterns, don't invent new ones

